Speaking as someone who's asc streak is a paltry 6 during the June
tourney,
a far cry from mrivan's 23, I would just like to opine that trap
searching is
_definitely_ an advisible tactic, one of many important survival tools.

Early on when i'm trying to ascend, I will usually search 4-6 times
before every
step when it is necessary, or even more times if I am weak. Obviously
you can
cut down on this by retracing steps, following your pet, using leash
detection, and
staying in corridors more. But a sleep trap, pit trap, or magic trap
can be an easy
instant kill, so it's totally necessary, even though you use up a lot
more food.

Also, to the OP, and contrary to others: there are certainly cases
where death
is totally unavoidable (yes, there really are). But these are pretty
rare. The
consensus is that with best play, %asc should be near 100. Yay nethack!

